===Etymology 1===
{{ja-kanjitab|ご|yomi=o}}
From {{bor|ja|ltc|-}} {{ltc-l|伍}}.

The numeral sense is a substitute spelling for {{ja-r|五|ご|[[five]]}}, likely borrowed from similar usage of written {{der|ja|zh|伍|tr=-||[[five]]}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{ja-pron|ご|acc=1}}

====Noun====
{{ja-noun|ご}}

# {{lb|ja|financial|archaic|sort=ご}} the number [[five]], [[5]] {{q|used only in legal documents, otherwise {{m|ja|五}}}}
# a [[military]] [[squad]] (usu. of five people); a [[group]]

=====Usage notes=====
Legal uses arose due to the relative ease with which certain number kanji can be fraudulently altered to look like other number kanji.  For instance, {{m|ja|三|tr=san||three}} could be modified to look like {{m|ja|五|tr=go||five}}, but it cannot be modified to look like {{m|ja|伍|tr=go||five|pos=in legal contexts}}.

