===Etymology===
From the initial ''*k''-series of Old Chinese third-person pronouns, cognate with {{och-l|其|id=2}}. Also compare {{cog|mkh-pro|*ge(e)ʔ}}, whence {{cog|km|គេ||they; he; she}} ({{zh-ref|Schuessler, 2007}}).

In standard Cantonese, the tone has been regularized by analogy with the other personal pronouns: {{zh-l|我|tr=ngo<sup>5</sup>}}, {{zh-l|你|tr=nei<sup>5</sup>}} ({{zh-ref|Li, 1965}}; {{zh-ref|Chan, 1998}}; {{zh-ref|Chang, 1999}}).

Before the use of {{zh-l|*佢}}, {{zh-l|*渠}} was also used in some novels and newspapers, such as {{zh-l|老婆奴續編}} (1926). The character {{lang|zh|渠}} is still preferred in lects such as Wu and sometimes Gan.

